{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not make for yourself molten elohim.</b> As you have done until now, when they made a molten calf — because they erred and entertained doubts about the attribute of Justice (din). Therefore Scripture joined to it the festival of matzot: ״תשמור״ — that they should remember the attribute of Mercy, for matzah is the attribute of Mercy, and they should not entertain doubts about the attribute of Justice. And set it upon your heart how He commanded here concerning matzah and warned concerning leaven: ״לא תשחט על חמץ״. And it appears to me to say that Scripture saw fit to explain that matzah and leaven allude to the attributes, and likewise the meat and the fat with which the passage was completed — therefore HaShem, may He be exalted, mentioned them to him in the passage of the Thirteen Attributes. And what you also find them (Exodus 22:24) in ״אם כסף תלוה״, in this very same section, is because there it began ״ששת ימים תעשה מעשיך וביום השביעי תשבות״, and it is known that the six days of Creation together with the Sabbath are the attributes, and these commandments are included among them — therefore He mentioned them there as well."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "הש\"י expanded as השם יתברך based on standard abbreviation in Rabbeinu Bahya; verse citation שמות כ״ב:כ״ד normalized to Exodus 22:24 (corresponds to Exodus 22:24 in some enumerations, Exodus 22:23 in others)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:00.019121937Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}